        "id": 127035,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-14T07:18:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I also spell out everything when texting, except LOL which I use very rarely... and ETA.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Going back to the card discussion</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I hate Infinitor and he should die horribly. My first game against him was H=3, so he started with 2 manisfestations. Then he played Insanity. By the time he was done with his first turn he had 9 manisfestations, two of which were occular swarms, and I took probably 30 total damage. By the end of round 3 he had played 11 of his 15 targets and my entire team was dead (Cap. Cosmic, Sky-scraper, and KNYFE)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, I haven't drawn many link cards for Skyscraper, but her other two forms are very powerful andI loved playing her with Cap's Augmented ally. Discard, use normal power to draw 2, play a huge card for some damage, then use thunder clap to hit al nonheroes for 2. Great times. My only issue is that the more universal damage she does with her huge form the more likely she is to injury her allies, one of her few +1 plays I saw immediately causes her to deal 1 damage to every ally. Good news is that Thorian monolith protects the team from that damage, bad news only for one turn. I can see why she's lv 3, since not only are you balancing her damage and flipping forms, but the linkage system is a little complex.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Actually, quick question, What happens to a link after the target is played in front of is destroyed. I've been playing that it stays out, but no longer does anything as it is not on a valid target but I would love some confirmation.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:01:34.798Z",
