      {
        "id": 127041,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-14T16:13:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"bloodylovelust\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/e68b1a/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> bloodylovelust:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It may be because I don't play on anything easier then advanced (some time add the powers from the additional sheet to make them even harder), but deadline is a pain. Even when you have ongoing destruction you have to debate if the 3 damage to hero targets is worth it.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Tempest is a godsend with advanced Deadline. Into the Stratosphere can buy you a free round, however its likely 4 or more enviro cards will be removed from the game if you do that. Limiting how fast the enviro deck empties per blast is key to slowing down his timer. Can't really afford having him blow up 4 cards more than once. It allows him one less flip cycle till the auto-lose condition.</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:01:35.251Z",
