      {
        "id": 127042,
        "name": "Blossercubbles",
        "username": "Blossercubbles",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/blossercubbles/{size}/1863_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-14T21:14:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I went to school for English, so the thought of using L33T SP34k or silly little not-words in the world of texting hurts my soul. I don't even know how to properly 'leet speak' as previously shown! And, since I'm not using my education for anything at all that I do, it's nice to pretend once in a while by always punctuating texts and e-mails appropriately.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>When I do abuse the language (and who doesn't?) I like to do so with tongue firmly planted in cheek. Or to be annoying. One of the two. Or Both! And how?</p>",
